# (after 0514) nvn/gw: the running-write page tables are 7-way set-associative and the storage-buffer write set grows (no more tainted conditional renders in high-draw scenes)
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/a67583a4f730a939928b33d92b8e6cbe81e28b8c  ("nvn/gw: make running-write tables set-associative and grow sbw")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-22 21:46 +0800; Co-authored-by: LZ
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); ported from seedds/nxnative, MIT. The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why: the direct-mapped running-write tables collapsed a slot on a 2-page hash collision to ~0 and latched it while GPU work stayed in flight; scenes with thousands of writable storage
#   buffers set g_sbw_over / g_gw_all and tainted conditional renders and partial uniform shadows: random or sustained black 3D frames behind the HUD (Donkey Kong Bananza, issue #2699).
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m; tests t_sbw, t_geometry): 128-byte-aligned 7-way set-associative tables with a per-set over_fence; g_gw merged into g_gwx plus a live-page check;
#   g_gwr a 1,024-set fast reject for the 4,096-entry report ring; g_sbwp / g_sbw_list grow at <= 50% load from 16,384 slots; SBW_WN 256.
# Games: Donkey Kong Bananza (040074A01BF12000) upstream; any game with many writable storage buffers. Switches: none. Applies as is (the review's candidate 0515).
# Tests (M1 Pro): t_sbw 49 checks, in HOST_TESTS. t_geometry's part not run: t_geometry.m does not compile on this tree (g_mdi_v, see build-host.sh). NOT run on a device.
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad; scripts/build-host.sh checks it).
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0514, in the order of the numbers of this folder (scripts/build-host.sh does).

